<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish road hauliers dispute resolved - media.</title>
<headline>Irish road hauliers dispute resolved - media.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Irish road hauliers dispute was resolved last night after improved pay rates from shipping companies were excepted in a secret ballot held in Dublin, Irish media reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Members of the Irish road haulage association voted by 2-to-1 to accept a new scheme of charges from up to 12 different shipping companies in Dublin port.</p>
<p>The hauliers have officially returned to work after a week-long dispute which brought freight movements to a halt.</p>
<p>Final details of the package will be agreed later on Wednesday, reports said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
